WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.260
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.530 --> 01:34.910
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.270 --> 01:37.789
[Episode 27]

4
01:38.789 --> 01:40.970
Even if I go to the General Political Department,

5
01:40.970 --> 01:43.700
aren't we still both in the Military Commission?

6
01:44.000 --> 01:46.060
There will always be chances to meet.

7
01:46.640 --> 01:48.150
When will that be?

8
01:49.640 --> 01:50.509
Miss me?

9
01:55.470 --> 01:56.600
Comrade Zhuangfei,

10
01:56.680 --> 01:59.200
could you write a few words of advice for me?

11
01:59.509 --> 02:00.400
Sure.

12
02:02.310 --> 02:05.150
Let me think about what to write.

13
02:04.910 --> 02:08.370
[Wei Yueqiao, Staff of the 2nd Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

14
02:08.150 --> 02:09.240
I got it.

15
02:10.120 --> 02:11.710
Our lives

16
02:12.470 --> 02:15.160
[Qian Zhuangfei, Deputy Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

17
02:13.190 --> 02:16.710
may be short and insignificant,

18
02:17.750 --> 02:20.470
but all great things

19
02:21.000 --> 02:24.870
are created by human hands.

20
02:26.280 --> 02:26.960
How is it?

21
02:27.040 --> 02:28.130
Good.

22
02:28.700 --> 02:30.050
In this life,

23
02:31.150 --> 02:36.710
one must realize this noble mission.

24
02:37.670 --> 02:41.480
That is the supreme joy

25
02:42.430 --> 02:46.030
in his life.

26
02:50.870 --> 02:52.329
You said that really well.

27
02:54.150 --> 02:55.430
I didn't say it.

28
02:56.400 --> 02:57.520
Turgenev did.

29
02:57.870 --> 02:58.630
Turgenev?

30
03:00.630 --> 03:01.960
I'll find a book for you.

31
03:06.870 --> 03:07.630
Rudin.

32
03:08.000 --> 03:08.800
It's yours.

33
03:09.240 --> 03:10.470
A novel by Turgenev!

34
03:10.870 --> 03:11.630
This book

35
03:11.910 --> 03:14.240
accompanied me from the areas under Nationalist control to the Soviet area.

36
03:14.240 --> 03:15.700
It's an old friend of mine.

37
03:15.850 --> 03:17.050
That's too precious.

38
03:17.710 --> 03:18.710
I can't accept it.

39
03:18.710 --> 03:19.560
Take it.

40
03:20.030 --> 03:21.520
I've read it many times.

41
03:23.680 --> 03:24.840
Then consider it a loan.

42
03:24.840 --> 03:25.720
When I finish copying it,

43
03:25.720 --> 03:27.430
I'll return it to you when we meet again.

44
03:27.430 --> 03:28.490
When we meet again,

45
03:28.560 --> 03:30.630
the revolution might have already succeeded.

46
03:30.630 --> 03:31.360
By then,

47
03:31.630 --> 03:34.030
you won't have to worry about buying a book.

48
03:35.480 --> 03:36.110
Wei,

49
03:37.240 --> 03:38.120
tell me.

50
03:39.000 --> 03:40.710
After the revolution succeeds,

51
03:40.710 --> 03:41.910
what do you want to do?

52
03:43.000 --> 03:44.730
When the revolution succeeds,

53
03:52.160 --> 03:54.690
I still want to go back to Lenin Primary School

54
03:54.910 --> 03:55.960
and be a teacher.

55
03:57.760 --> 03:58.690
Tell me about it.

56
04:01.900 --> 04:04.730
I want to have a clean desk

57
04:05.190 --> 04:06.790
with my favorite books on it.

58
04:07.030 --> 04:08.160
In front of the desk,

59
04:08.280 --> 04:09.880
there should be a big window.

60
04:11.310 --> 04:11.910
When preparing lessons,

61
04:11.910 --> 04:13.110
sitting at this desk,

62
04:13.190 --> 04:14.790
I can look through the window

63
04:15.360 --> 04:17.269
and see the sun rise

64
04:18.240 --> 04:19.160
and set,

65
04:19.510 --> 04:21.120
the moon rise and set.

66
04:21.829 --> 04:23.230
Every time class is over,

67
04:23.510 --> 04:24.870
I'll sit at this desk

68
04:25.480 --> 04:27.140
and wash off all the chalk dust

69
04:27.310 --> 04:28.390
from my body.

70
04:28.610 --> 04:30.870
I'll take the tea from the back hill of my hometown,

71
04:30.870 --> 04:32.830
boil some mountain spring water,

72
04:33.070 --> 04:34.390
take a big glass,

73
04:34.680 --> 04:36.000
throw in a handful of tea,

74
04:36.000 --> 04:37.070
and pour the boiling water

75
04:37.070 --> 04:37.930
into the glass.

76
04:38.360 --> 04:40.420
I'll watch the tea leaves in the glass

77
04:40.670 --> 04:42.630
tumbling in the sunlight,

78
04:43.000 --> 04:44.659
and then slowly falling down.

79
04:44.800 --> 04:46.200
If you just tap the glass,

80
04:46.760 --> 04:48.560
the tea leaves float up gently.

81
04:49.120 --> 04:50.450
Looking at it like this,

82
04:51.720 --> 04:54.390
the tea fuzz is really beautiful.

83
04:55.040 --> 04:56.440
Then I'll take a nice sip,

84
04:57.190 --> 05:00.560
thinking about what the children want to learn tomorrow,

85
05:00.950 --> 05:02.680
what they are willing to learn.

86
05:04.870 --> 05:06.470
That's what I want to do most.

87
05:07.160 --> 05:08.160
Don't laugh at me.

88
05:09.160 --> 05:10.160
Why would I?

89
05:10.830 --> 05:11.600
Wei,

90
05:11.920 --> 05:13.840
your dream is very beautiful.

91
05:15.430 --> 05:16.560
Comrade Zhuangfei,

92
05:16.950 --> 05:17.870
when we win,

93
05:18.070 --> 05:19.270
what do you want to do?

94
05:21.270 --> 05:22.680
I still want to make movies.

95
05:22.680 --> 05:23.480
Make movies?

96
05:23.720 --> 05:24.450
Make movies.

97
05:24.680 --> 05:25.580
I've made movies before.

98
05:25.580 --> 05:26.510
You didn't know?

99
05:26.800 --> 05:27.730
Back in Peiping,

100
05:28.000 --> 05:29.720
Hu Di and I made a movie,

101
05:30.430 --> 05:31.560
a martial arts film,

102
05:31.560 --> 05:33.680
called "The Hidden Hero of Yanshan."

103
05:34.190 --> 05:34.960
The Hidden Hero of Yanshan.

104
05:34.960 --> 05:36.190
I even brought my daughter along

105
05:36.190 --> 05:37.630
to play a role in it.

106
05:38.120 --> 05:39.680
Hu Di played a martial arts hero.

107
05:39.680 --> 05:41.090
He later got a nickname,

108
05:41.120 --> 05:43.950
"the Oriental Fairbanks."

109
05:44.120 --> 05:45.120
Fairbanks.

110
05:48.070 --> 05:50.870
But if we make movies again after the victory,

111
05:51.630 --> 05:53.480
I won't make martial arts films anymore.

112
05:53.480 --> 05:54.630
Then what do you want to film?

113
05:54.630 --> 05:56.760
I want to film our western expedition,

114
05:57.540 --> 05:59.740
the western expedition of the Red Army.

115
05:59.830 --> 06:02.560
I want to film how many mountains we've crossed,

116
06:03.560 --> 06:05.600
how many rivers we've waded through,

117
06:05.600 --> 06:07.920
and how many battles and sacrifices we've had.

118
06:07.920 --> 06:09.380
I want to film all of these.

119
06:09.720 --> 06:11.180
I also want to film Ruijin,

120
06:11.670 --> 06:12.670
your hometown.

121
06:13.310 --> 06:14.270
Wei, do you know

122
06:14.560 --> 06:16.590
how I felt when I first arrived

123
06:16.610 --> 06:17.670
in the Soviet area?

124
06:18.510 --> 06:19.430
Free.

125
06:20.600 --> 06:21.630
Safe.

126
06:22.430 --> 06:23.660
Because I was home.

127
06:24.560 --> 06:26.750
During those years working in the areas under Nationalist control,

128
06:26.750 --> 06:28.210
every day I opened my eyes,

129
06:28.870 --> 06:30.680
every nerve of mine was tense.

130
06:31.870 --> 06:33.000
I was terrified that

131
06:33.720 --> 06:35.040
any slight oversight

132
06:35.330 --> 06:36.770
would expose me.

133
06:38.000 --> 06:39.040
But that day,

134
06:39.720 --> 06:41.120
riding a big white horse,

135
06:42.360 --> 06:44.159
I galloped all the way to Ruijin.

136
06:44.630 --> 06:46.159
The sky was so blue that day,

137
06:46.590 --> 06:48.050
and the wind was so gentle.

138
06:48.159 --> 06:49.680
At a glance, I saw that

139
06:50.240 --> 06:52.510
big camphor tree outside our central government.

140
06:52.510 --> 06:53.270
I was overjoyed!

141
06:53.270 --> 06:53.920
I jumped

142
06:54.070 --> 06:55.210
off my horse at once,

143
06:55.240 --> 06:56.700
and I eagerly threw myself

144
06:58.040 --> 06:59.430
face down on the grass!

145
06:59.750 --> 07:00.560
I turned over,

146
07:00.830 --> 07:02.120
spread my limbs out,

147
07:02.250 --> 07:04.290
and lay there like a big star!

148
07:04.830 --> 07:07.600
The sunlight filtered through the branches

149
07:08.030 --> 07:09.210
and shone on my face.

150
07:09.480 --> 07:11.480
It was so dazzling that I shed tears.

151
07:11.610 --> 07:12.930
I used all my strength

152
07:13.310 --> 07:14.820
and shouted at the top of my lungs!

153
07:14.820 --> 07:15.950
I said one sentence!

154
07:17.000 --> 07:18.000
Guess what it was.

155
07:18.430 --> 07:19.360
What did you say?

156
07:19.680 --> 07:24.920
I am a Communist Party member!

157
07:30.730 --> 07:31.860
Comrade Zhuangfei,

158
07:32.270 --> 07:35.470
can you take me with you when you make movies in the future?

159
07:36.720 --> 07:37.920
I'll take you with me!

160
07:38.680 --> 07:39.600
Write it well.

161
07:39.870 --> 07:40.680
Use your pen

162
07:40.860 --> 07:43.360
to turn what you've seen

163
07:43.800 --> 07:45.630
and experienced on this western expedition

164
07:45.630 --> 07:46.630
into good stories

165
07:47.159 --> 07:48.040
for movies!

166
07:48.270 --> 07:50.170
Okay, for movies!

167
07:53.280 --> 07:54.040
Cheers.

168
08:01.750 --> 08:03.560
Doesn't this plain water

169
08:03.950 --> 08:04.920
taste a bit like

170
08:05.190 --> 08:06.960
the tea from your hometown now?

171
08:30.040 --> 08:33.690
[Mountainous areas, Guizhou]

172
08:43.990 --> 08:45.230
No supplies,

173
08:45.310 --> 08:46.380
no rest,

174
08:46.890 --> 08:48.080
just keep walking like this.

175
08:48.080 --> 08:49.320
And we keep backtracking.

176
08:49.320 --> 08:50.360
Walking like this every day,

177
08:50.360 --> 08:51.800
when will it end?

178
08:52.510 --> 08:53.750
No fighting, just walking,

179
08:53.750 --> 08:55.010
we'll be dragged down.

180
08:56.910 --> 08:57.870
Didn't we say before

181
08:57.870 --> 08:59.740
that we were going to cross the Yangtze River to the north?

182
08:59.740 --> 09:00.870
Why does it feel like

183
09:00.990 --> 09:02.790
we're just going in circles now?

184
09:03.200 --> 09:04.010
All units,

185
09:04.480 --> 09:05.190
rest on the spot!

186
09:05.190 --> 09:06.310
All units,

187
09:06.530 --> 09:08.530
take shelter from the rain!

188
09:09.240 --> 09:10.120
When resting,

189
09:10.720 --> 09:12.000
don't just sit there!

190
09:12.000 --> 09:12.790
All units,

191
09:12.910 --> 09:14.220
loosen your puttees,

192
09:14.630 --> 09:16.830
and pop the blood blisters on your feet.

193
09:17.520 --> 09:20.070
You must protect your feet!

194
09:20.630 --> 09:21.870
If your feet are ruined,

195
09:21.870 --> 09:23.270
you won't be able to walk!

196
09:24.120 --> 09:25.390
Loosen your puttees!

197
09:25.410 --> 09:26.630
Come in and take shelter from the rain!

198
09:26.630 --> 09:27.960
Come, everyone come in.

199
09:28.750 --> 09:30.010
Come, come in quickly!

200
09:30.030 --> 09:30.890
Move inside!

201
09:38.270 --> 09:39.390
Comrades,

202
09:40.910 --> 09:43.200
I'll tell you a story!

203
09:43.200 --> 09:44.030
How about that?

204
09:44.030 --> 09:45.310
Sounds good!

205
09:45.970 --> 09:47.230
Commander-in-Chief,

206
09:47.240 --> 09:49.100
which part are you telling today?

207
09:49.550 --> 09:50.780
What do you all want to hear?

208
09:50.780 --> 09:52.370
Romance of the Three Kingdoms!

209
09:52.370 --> 09:54.100
Romance of the Three Kingdoms!

210
09:54.120 --> 09:56.080
Alright, then today I'll tell

211
09:56.080 --> 09:57.630
a story of making a feint to the east and attacking in the west,

212
09:57.630 --> 09:59.990
Cao Mengde's surprise attack on Baima City.

213
09:59.990 --> 10:01.350
Good!

214
10:05.850 --> 10:06.940
It is said that

215
10:07.670 --> 10:09.470
in the late Eastern Han Dynasty,

216
10:10.030 --> 10:11.550
Yuan Shao, the warlord of Hebei,

217
10:11.550 --> 10:12.910
and Cao Cao, the warlord of the Central Plains,

218
10:12.910 --> 10:14.840
fought the Battle of Guandu.

219
10:15.190 --> 10:18.250
At that time, Yuan Shao had many soldiers and generals.

220
10:18.600 --> 10:20.000
He had an army of 110,000.

221
10:20.360 --> 10:21.270
And Cao Cao

222
10:21.720 --> 10:23.630
had only 20,000 men.

223
10:23.830 --> 10:25.150
20,000 against 110,000.

224
10:25.150 --> 10:26.720
That's not as dangerous as our situation.

225
10:26.720 --> 10:28.150
Right, not as dangerous as ours.

226
10:28.150 --> 10:30.200
Don't interrupt. Listen to the Commander-in-Chief.

227
10:30.200 --> 10:31.480
Not long after the war started,

228
10:31.480 --> 10:33.600
Yuan Shao sent three generals

229
10:34.150 --> 10:34.960
to lead troops

230
10:35.320 --> 10:38.510
and surround Cao Cao's important town, Baima.

231
10:38.960 --> 10:40.820
One of the generals was Yan Liang.

232
10:41.200 --> 10:42.750
The governor defending Baima, Liu Yan,

233
10:42.750 --> 10:44.030
knowing he was no match,

234
10:44.030 --> 10:46.910
quickly sent someone to ask Cao Cao for help.

235
10:47.670 --> 10:48.480
Baima

236
10:48.720 --> 10:50.270
was Cao Cao's northern gate.

237
10:50.270 --> 10:52.070
It absolutely could not be lost.

238
10:52.550 --> 10:53.610
Cao Cao was anxious

239
10:53.890 --> 10:56.090
and wanted to lead troops to the rescue.

240
10:56.200 --> 10:57.630
But at that time, Cao Cao

241
10:57.710 --> 10:59.110
didn't have many troops.

242
10:59.240 --> 11:00.510
Once he went to the rescue,

243
11:00.510 --> 11:02.000
he would be dragged down by Yuan Shao's army,

244
11:02.000 --> 11:04.470
and his whole army might be wiped out.

245
11:04.510 --> 11:05.670
What could be done?

246
11:06.510 --> 11:07.220
Commander-in-Chief,

247
11:07.220 --> 11:08.750
how did Cao Cao finally break the siege?

248
11:08.750 --> 11:09.170
Right.

249
11:09.200 --> 11:10.320
How did he break the siege?

250
11:10.320 --> 11:12.000
How did he break the siege?

251
11:12.000 --> 11:13.460
How did he break the siege?

252
11:13.550 --> 11:15.360
Cao Cao had an advisor

253
11:15.600 --> 11:16.630
named Xun You.

254
11:16.910 --> 11:18.170
He gave Cao Cao an idea.

255
11:18.510 --> 11:19.100
He said,

256
11:19.630 --> 11:21.000
with our current forces,

257
11:21.000 --> 11:22.460
to lift the siege of Baima,

258
11:22.550 --> 11:25.670
we must divide Yuan Shao's forces.

259
11:26.720 --> 11:29.480
There is a place west of Baima called Yanjin,

260
11:30.270 --> 11:32.330
which leads to Yuan Shao's rear base.

261
11:32.390 --> 11:34.720
If we pretend to attack Yanjin,

262
11:34.910 --> 11:36.100
Yuan Shao will definitely be anxious.

263
11:36.100 --> 11:36.730
Once he is anxious,

264
11:36.730 --> 11:38.720
he will definitely send troops to the rescue.

265
11:38.720 --> 11:42.710
So where are the troops closest to Yanjin?

266
11:43.300 --> 11:44.940
Of course, it's Baima!

267
11:47.340 --> 11:48.730
Did Yuan Shao fall for it?

268
11:48.730 --> 11:49.870
If Yuan Shao didn't fall for it,

269
11:49.870 --> 11:50.790
there wouldn't be the later

270
11:50.790 --> 11:54.120
story of making a feint to the east and attacking in the west.

271
11:54.320 --> 11:55.180
Just like that,

272
11:55.390 --> 11:57.320
Cao Cao acted according to the plan

273
11:57.390 --> 11:59.920
and went to attack Yanjin with great fanfare.

274
12:00.360 --> 12:02.000
Yuan Shao indeed fell for it

275
12:02.360 --> 12:05.490
and diverted most of his forces from Baima to the rescue.

276
12:06.320 --> 12:07.150
And in Baima,

277
12:07.410 --> 12:08.570
he only left behind

278
12:08.600 --> 12:10.360
the brave but foolish Yan Liang.

279
12:10.360 --> 12:14.400
Cao Cao personally led 5,000 light cavalry to raid Baima.

280
12:14.710 --> 12:16.870
Yan Liang hastily engaged in battle, caught off guard,

281
12:16.870 --> 12:18.670
and was cut down by Guan Yunchang

282
12:19.360 --> 12:20.750
from his horse with a single strike!

283
12:20.750 --> 12:22.320
Good, good, good!

284
12:22.320 --> 12:23.670
Tell another one!

285
12:24.030 --> 12:25.030
Tell another one!

286
12:25.270 --> 12:26.550
One more!

287
12:26.570 --> 12:28.240
Commander-in-Chief Zhu, tell another one!

288
12:28.240 --> 12:28.960
One more!

289
12:28.980 --> 12:29.630
One more!

290
12:29.630 --> 12:30.160
One more!

291
12:30.170 --> 12:31.100
Comrade Zedong,

292
12:31.200 --> 12:32.240
Commander-in-Chief.

293
12:32.240 --> 12:32.930
Vice Chairman Zhou.

294
12:32.930 --> 12:33.650
Vice Chairman Zhou.

295
12:33.650 --> 12:35.910
Vice Chairman Zhou! Vice Chairman Zhou!

296
12:36.080 --> 12:36.640
Comrade Zedong,

297
12:36.640 --> 12:37.720
Commander-in-Chief,

298
12:37.720 --> 12:40.050
there is a new enemy intelligence report.

299
12:40.240 --> 12:41.360
Are there any changes?

300
12:41.360 --> 12:43.620
Chiang Kai-shek has arrived in Guiyang.

301
12:44.000 --> 12:44.670
Chairman.

302
12:44.880 --> 12:47.920
This is Chiang Kai-shek's latest combat deployment.

303
12:55.160 --> 12:58.000
This Chiang is still using that fortress tactic.

304
12:58.390 --> 12:59.290
Little does he know,

305
12:59.290 --> 13:00.560
while trapping us,

306
13:00.840 --> 13:02.440
he also trapped his own troops,

307
13:02.440 --> 13:03.710
which gave us a perfect

308
13:03.740 --> 13:04.620
gap to escape.

309
13:04.910 --> 13:06.370
Chairman, you are right.

310
13:06.870 --> 13:08.670
Currently, the Kuomintang army's defense line

311
13:08.670 --> 13:10.080
has not been fully formed.

312
13:10.080 --> 13:11.610
Between Yaxi and Bailakan,

313
13:11.670 --> 13:12.470
there is a gap.

314
13:12.720 --> 13:14.180
We can pass through there.

315
13:15.480 --> 13:16.410
The question is,

316
13:16.750 --> 13:18.010
after we pass through,

317
13:18.180 --> 13:19.840
which direction should we go?

318
13:19.840 --> 13:21.240
Southeast or southwest?

319
13:23.960 --> 13:27.020
The Commander-in-Chief has already given the answer.

320
13:27.360 --> 13:27.880
Me?

321
13:27.980 --> 13:28.530
Yes.

322
13:28.670 --> 13:30.160
Without feigning an attack on Yanjin,

323
13:30.160 --> 13:32.110
forces in Baima wouldn't have been divided.

324
13:32.110 --> 13:33.890
You mean making a feint to the east and attacking in the west?

325
13:33.890 --> 13:34.520
Yes.

326
13:34.870 --> 13:37.340
You two shouldn't speak in riddles.

327
13:37.700 --> 13:38.460
Mao,

328
13:38.540 --> 13:40.400
you'd better explain it clearly.

329
13:42.260 --> 13:43.060
This is Shatu.

330
13:44.320 --> 13:45.150
This is Andi.

331
13:45.790 --> 13:46.870
This is the Wujiang River.

332
13:46.870 --> 13:48.870
Change a one-step jump into a two-step jump,

333
13:48.870 --> 13:51.150
break through the Zunyi-Renhuai blockade,

334
13:51.150 --> 13:53.480
and assemble the troops at Shatu and Andi.

335
13:53.750 --> 13:56.780
Then look for an opportunity to cross the Wujiang River southward,

336
13:56.780 --> 13:57.840
and head to Qiannan.

337
13:57.840 --> 13:58.650
Qiannan?

338
13:59.010 --> 14:02.070
But that's the focus of the Kuomintang army's defense.

339
14:02.120 --> 14:03.320
Maneuvering there

340
14:03.360 --> 14:05.860
will be even harder than in northern Guizhou.

341
14:05.860 --> 14:07.740
Of course, we shouldn't stay long in Qiannan,

342
14:07.740 --> 14:09.510
but we can draw out the Yunnan Army.

343
14:09.510 --> 14:11.000
If the Yunnan Army doesn't enter Guizhou,

344
14:11.000 --> 14:12.400
we have no way out.

345
14:15.510 --> 14:16.910
This is a brilliant move,

346
14:17.390 --> 14:18.600
but also a risky one.

347
14:19.360 --> 14:20.000
Everyone,

348
14:20.270 --> 14:22.800
if we don't play it well, it could be a dead end.

349
14:23.250 --> 14:24.910
But if we don't make this move,

350
14:25.110 --> 14:27.030
we won't be able to shake off Chiang Kai-shek's

351
14:27.030 --> 14:29.600
400,000-strong army pursuing and intercepting us.

352
14:29.600 --> 14:31.930
At this critical moment of life and death,

353
14:32.170 --> 14:34.500
only by taking a risky move can we survive.

354
14:37.050 --> 14:39.580
Chairman, after drawing out the Yunnan Army,

355
14:39.790 --> 14:40.860
where do we go?

356
15:13.630 --> 15:14.400
Let's go.

357
15:16.220 --> 15:18.620
On March 28, 1935,

358
15:19.220 --> 15:21.930
covered by the 9th Red Army Corps' feint

359
15:21.960 --> 15:24.110
toward Changgan Mountain and Fengxiangba,

360
15:24.110 --> 15:25.680
the main force of the Central Red Army,

361
15:25.680 --> 15:27.440
braving the fierce wind and rain,

362
15:27.440 --> 15:29.770
slipped through a gap less than 15 li wide

363
15:29.800 --> 15:31.400
in the Kuomintang blockade

364
15:31.480 --> 15:34.370
between Yaxi and Bailakan,

365
15:34.920 --> 15:36.600
entered the Shatu and Andi areas

366
15:36.600 --> 15:38.590
on the north bank of the Wujiang River,

367
15:38.590 --> 15:41.290
and began preparations to cross the Wujiang River southward.

368
15:41.290 --> 15:43.670
At that time, people probably wouldn't have thought

369
15:43.670 --> 15:45.870
that on the north bank of the Wujiang River over 90 years ago,

370
15:45.870 --> 15:47.910
on this unknown mountain road,

371
15:48.150 --> 15:51.750
Mao Zedong's shocking stroke with a bamboo pole

372
15:52.080 --> 15:53.220
would change the fate of

373
15:53.220 --> 15:54.720
the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army

374
15:54.720 --> 15:56.880
and even the Chinese revolution.

375
16:00.300 --> 16:05.500
[Mao Guangxiang Mansion, Guiyang, Guizhou]

376
16:00.520 --> 16:01.600
The Generalissimo believes

377
16:01.600 --> 16:04.080
that the Zhu-Mao Communist army is at the end of its tether

378
16:04.080 --> 16:06.010
and has now been forced to flee into Guizhou.

379
16:06.010 --> 16:08.300
The vast Yangtze River is like a natural moat,

380
16:08.300 --> 16:10.750
and the Communist army has not yet determined a crossing point.

381
16:10.750 --> 16:11.800
Intercepted in the front

382
16:11.800 --> 16:13.120
and pursued from behind,

383
16:13.120 --> 16:16.120
with our mountain blockhouses scattered like stars,

384
16:16.360 --> 16:19.250
Zhu and Mao have indeed reached a dead end.

385
16:19.330 --> 16:21.140
[Chen Cheng, Commander-in-Chief of the Kuomintang Army's Reserve Forces in Jiangxi]

386
16:19.440 --> 16:21.300
Now we just need to tighten the encirclement

387
16:21.300 --> 16:23.360
[Yan Daogang, Director of the Aide-de-Camp Office of the Generalissimo of the Military Affairs Commission of the Nationalist Government]

388
16:21.340 --> 16:24.340
to catch the Zhu-Mao Communist army in one fell swoop.

389
16:28.510 --> 16:29.440
Generalissimo,

390
16:29.440 --> 16:30.900
if you have no objections,

391
16:31.240 --> 16:32.240
I will publish it.

392
16:32.360 --> 16:33.490
In the past few days,

393
16:33.670 --> 16:35.870
battle reports have been pouring in from all sides.

394
16:35.870 --> 16:38.540
Some say the Communist army will cross north into Sichuan,

395
16:38.540 --> 16:40.060
[Xue Yue, Commander-in-chief of the 2nd Army Group of the KMT's Pursuit Army]

396
16:38.790 --> 16:41.450
while others say they will flee east into Hunan.

397
16:42.270 --> 16:42.870
Also,

398
16:42.940 --> 16:45.510
Pan Wenhua of the Sichuan Army sent a telegram,

399
16:45.510 --> 16:47.550
saying the Communist army has crossed the Zunren Road

400
16:47.550 --> 16:49.030
and is fleeing south.

401
16:49.600 --> 16:51.030
I want to ask you all,

402
16:52.030 --> 16:54.150
where exactly is the Communist army?

403
16:54.300 --> 16:56.700
How many main forces do they actually have?

404
16:57.210 --> 17:00.110
Whether the Zhu-Mao Communist army crosses north

405
17:00.240 --> 17:01.080
or flees east,

406
17:01.270 --> 17:02.470
they cannot succeed.

407
17:03.030 --> 17:04.310
Unless they really cross

408
17:04.310 --> 17:06.170
the Zunren Road and flee south...

409
17:06.480 --> 17:08.010
That would be real trouble.

410
17:08.480 --> 17:09.329
So I think

411
17:09.359 --> 17:11.839
we should order the two columns of Zhou Hunyuan and Wu Qiwei

412
17:11.839 --> 17:14.290
to advance towards Panshui and Xinchang,

413
17:14.640 --> 17:16.480
casting a wide net to catch the big fish.

414
17:16.480 --> 17:17.410
But if we do that,

415
17:17.609 --> 17:19.829
the flanks of the two columns will lose their protection.

416
17:19.829 --> 17:21.790
If the Communist army launches a surprise attack,

417
17:21.790 --> 17:23.440
the consequences would be disastrous.

418
17:23.440 --> 17:24.569
That's impossible.

419
17:24.609 --> 17:26.280
Isn't Sun Du's unit of the Yunnan Army

420
17:26.280 --> 17:29.670
between Maobachang and Wumakou?

421
17:30.880 --> 17:31.810
Generalissimo,

422
17:32.190 --> 17:34.040
Sun Du hasn't moved at all.

423
17:35.730 --> 17:37.640
Your telegraphic order was sent long ago,

424
17:37.640 --> 17:39.510
but Long Yun doesn't seem very active.

425
17:39.510 --> 17:41.720
He keeps using the excuse of preventing the Communist army from fleeing west

426
17:41.720 --> 17:44.580
and is unwilling to mobilize Sun Du to advance east.

427
17:44.960 --> 17:46.430
Each has their own hidden agenda!

428
17:46.430 --> 17:48.430
This is the Party's greatest enemy!

429
17:49.350 --> 17:50.280
Telegraph Sun Du.

430
17:50.280 --> 17:51.940
Send him a telegram in my name.

431
17:52.000 --> 17:52.960
Before the 31st,

432
17:53.310 --> 17:55.070
have him rush to the area between Daguxinchang

433
17:55.070 --> 17:56.070
and Xi'anzhai

434
17:56.240 --> 17:57.350
to set up a defense line

435
17:57.350 --> 17:59.320
to protect the flanks of Zhou Hunyuan and Wu Qiwei.

436
17:59.320 --> 17:59.870
Yes.

437
18:05.370 --> 18:06.300
Generalissimo.

438
18:06.480 --> 18:07.550
Let's go inside first.

439
18:07.550 --> 18:08.550
The rain is so heavy,

440
18:08.550 --> 18:09.810
don't get caught in it.

441
18:15.540 --> 18:17.570
I hope this rainstorm

442
18:18.390 --> 18:21.250
will also smash down on the Communist army's heads.

443
18:31.190 --> 18:35.660
[Shatu Town, the north shore of Wujiang River, Guizhou]

444
18:53.360 --> 18:55.020
Everyone, don't stay silent.

445
18:55.330 --> 18:57.130
Let's continue the discussion.

446
18:57.290 --> 18:59.010
Today is a Zhuge Liang meeting.

447
18:59.010 --> 19:00.540
We, this group of cobblers,

448
19:00.650 --> 19:02.310
must all become Zhuge Liangs.

449
19:02.380 --> 19:03.440
Everyone, keep thinking.

450
19:03.440 --> 19:05.840
We will definitely come up with a solution.

451
19:06.760 --> 19:08.620
Can the 9th Corps coordinate a bit

452
19:08.860 --> 19:11.720
[Ye Jianying, Chief of Staff of the 3rd Red Army Corps]

453
19:09.100 --> 19:10.160
and find a way to draw away

454
19:10.160 --> 19:12.760
the six divisions of Zhou Hunyuan and Wu Qiwei?

455
19:12.790 --> 19:14.190
We have considered this.

456
19:14.680 --> 19:16.070
The position of the 9th Corps

457
19:16.070 --> 19:18.550
is right between the armies of Zhou and Wu.

458
19:19.330 --> 19:20.330
They can't move.

459
19:20.510 --> 19:22.510
Then can we delay crossing the river

460
19:22.590 --> 19:24.000
and wait for the two columns of Zhou and Wu to pass

461
19:24.000 --> 19:24.920
before taking action?

462
19:24.920 --> 19:25.720
It's too late.

463
19:26.070 --> 19:27.750
The troops have already assembled by the river.

464
19:27.750 --> 19:29.210
If we don't cross quickly,

465
19:29.310 --> 19:30.830
once discovered by the enemy,

466
19:30.830 --> 19:32.830
we will risk being forced into a desperate last stand.

467
19:32.830 --> 19:35.450
Then let's cross the river as soon as possible according to the original plan.

468
19:35.450 --> 19:37.210
The enemy might not discover us.

469
19:37.210 --> 19:38.270
Crossing the river

470
19:38.330 --> 19:40.270
requires seizing the ferry crossing.

471
19:40.270 --> 19:41.670
It can't be done silently.

472
19:41.670 --> 19:44.470
It will take us two to three days to cross the river.

473
19:44.670 --> 19:46.470
Once the enemy pursues us,

474
19:46.850 --> 19:49.510
we run the risk of being attacked mid-crossing.

475
19:49.830 --> 19:50.510
Besides,

476
19:50.640 --> 19:53.630
the three enemy divisions on the south bank will act at the slightest sign.

477
19:53.630 --> 19:54.390
At that time,

478
19:54.590 --> 19:57.090
the Wujiang River is very likely to become the Xiang River.

479
19:57.090 --> 19:59.090
It might be even more severe than the Xiang River.

480
19:59.090 --> 20:00.330
Our time is tighter,

481
20:00.770 --> 20:01.900
the enemy is closer,

482
20:02.110 --> 20:04.310
the space on both sides of the Wujiang River is narrower,

483
20:04.310 --> 20:06.440
and our forces are more concentrated.

484
20:06.550 --> 20:08.070
Once attacked from both sides by the enemy,

485
20:08.070 --> 20:09.880
the consequences will be disastrous.

486
20:09.880 --> 20:11.190
Crossing the river isn't right,

487
20:11.190 --> 20:12.640
and not crossing isn't right either.

488
20:12.640 --> 20:14.100
Aren't we in a dilemma now?

489
20:25.640 --> 20:26.900
I said something useless.

490
20:26.900 --> 20:27.900
It's not useless.

491
20:29.320 --> 20:30.950
Everything we say today will be useful.

492
20:30.840 --> 20:33.890
[Zeng Xisheng, Director of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

493
20:31.480 --> 20:32.610
What we need to do now

494
20:33.000 --> 20:34.000
is to find a way

495
20:34.440 --> 20:37.790
to draw away the troops of Zhou Hunyuan and Wu Qiwei.

496
20:38.200 --> 20:39.660
Let's just focus on this problem and think it through.

497
20:39.660 --> 20:41.310
How can we focus on this problem?

498
20:41.310 --> 20:42.110
Unless we have

499
20:42.130 --> 20:45.060
Chiang Kai-shek's military tally to deploy troops.

500
20:48.610 --> 20:50.410
I said something useless again.

501
20:50.680 --> 20:51.920
No, no.

502
20:51.980 --> 20:53.110
This is not useless.

503
20:53.510 --> 20:55.520
What if we forge a military tally?

504
20:56.030 --> 20:57.920
Isn't Zhuge Liangs holding a meeting today?

505
20:57.920 --> 20:59.110
We cobblers

506
20:59.110 --> 21:00.510
must become Zhuge Liangs.

507
21:00.510 --> 21:02.910
Zhuge Liang once forged military tallies.

508
21:03.060 --> 21:03.720
A telegram?

509
21:04.240 --> 21:04.790
Yes.

510
21:05.160 --> 21:06.690
We'll forge a fake telegram

511
21:06.990 --> 21:08.550
in the name of Chiang Kai-shek,

512
21:08.550 --> 21:09.610
bypassing Xue Yue,

513
21:09.760 --> 21:11.790
and directly order Zhou Hunyuan and Wu Qiwei

514
21:11.790 --> 21:13.590
to change their marching route.

515
21:14.960 --> 21:17.250
This time Chiang is supervising the battle in Guiyang,

516
21:17.250 --> 21:18.510
attending to everything personally.

517
21:18.510 --> 21:21.310
Bypassing the chain of command is commonplace for him.

518
21:21.310 --> 21:23.110
It's theoretically feasible.

519
21:23.440 --> 21:25.640
Can the Second Bureau make it look real?

520
21:26.600 --> 21:27.320
No problem!

521
21:27.720 --> 21:29.480
We often decipher the enemy's telegrams,

522
21:29.480 --> 21:31.110
and are familiar with the Central Army's cipher procedures

523
21:31.110 --> 21:31.920
and patterns.

524
21:32.200 --> 21:34.590
The enemy uses both dedicated and general codebooks,

525
21:34.590 --> 21:35.350
and we have both.

526
21:35.350 --> 21:38.240
The enemy telegraphers' usual techniques

527
21:38.260 --> 21:38.940
and rhythms,

528
21:38.940 --> 21:40.160
we are familiar with them all.

529
21:40.160 --> 21:40.590
Also,

530
21:40.680 --> 21:42.750
regarding Chiang Kai-shek's telegram rhetoric and format,

531
21:42.750 --> 21:44.550
Comrade Zhuangfei is an expert.

532
21:45.270 --> 21:46.070
It can be done.

533
21:47.550 --> 21:48.880
Absolutely no problem.

534
21:49.140 --> 21:49.760
Good!

535
21:51.860 --> 21:53.480
Then we'll use the cipher in reverse.

536
21:53.480 --> 21:55.920
Your Second Bureau will act as a lantern,

537
21:56.480 --> 21:58.110
but this time it shines on the enemy.

538
21:58.110 --> 21:59.920
Shine it well and carefully.

539
22:00.880 --> 22:03.680
Strive to shine Zhou Hunyuan and Wu Qiwei's troops

540
22:03.880 --> 22:04.790
into a pit.

541
22:05.160 --> 22:05.880
Mao,

542
22:06.920 --> 22:07.880
what is your pit?

543
22:08.090 --> 22:10.530
Where do you plan to lead

544
22:10.790 --> 22:11.720
Zhou and Wu's two columns?

545
22:11.720 --> 22:12.980
I haven't decided yet.

546
22:13.070 --> 22:13.880
But I think

547
22:14.160 --> 22:16.110
if we temporarily change their marching plan,

548
22:16.110 --> 22:18.070
once Zhou and Wu suspect and verify it,

549
22:18.070 --> 22:19.400
it will be troublesome.

550
22:19.590 --> 22:22.250
I think we shouldn't change the marching route.

551
22:22.310 --> 22:23.720
Just urge them to move faster.

552
22:23.720 --> 22:25.750
The faster they go, the further they are from us.

553
22:25.750 --> 22:27.680
This is also Chiang's recent norm,

554
22:27.810 --> 22:29.480
so it won't easily arouse suspicion.

555
22:29.480 --> 22:30.240
Good pit.

556
22:31.240 --> 22:31.970
The telegram

557
22:32.140 --> 22:34.400
will be drafted according to Comrade Zedong's opinion.

558
22:34.400 --> 22:35.400
Comrade Xisheng,

559
22:35.480 --> 22:36.610
Comrade Zhuangfei,

560
22:36.750 --> 22:38.640
you must think it through carefully.

561
22:38.640 --> 22:40.500
A trump card can only be used once.

562
22:41.110 --> 22:41.960
If it fails

563
22:42.270 --> 22:43.730
and the enemy suspects it,

564
22:43.750 --> 22:45.270
the future work of our Second Bureau

565
22:45.270 --> 22:46.600
will be very difficult.

566
22:47.070 --> 22:48.440
Please rest assured, leaders.

567
22:48.440 --> 22:50.770
We are confident in completing this task,

568
22:51.960 --> 22:53.620
ensuring nothing goes wrong.

569
23:05.490 --> 23:08.290
Go send a telegram to Dong Zhentang and Li Zhuoran.

570
23:08.510 --> 23:11.310
Tell their 5th Corps that on the outskirts of Andi Town,

571
23:11.310 --> 23:14.200
along the Kuchayuan line, they must rush to build field fortifications,

572
23:14.110 --> 23:16.320
[Wang Zheng, Director of the Third Bureau of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

573
23:14.750 --> 23:15.550
just in case.

574
23:15.930 --> 23:18.640
In case the Second Bureau's method doesn't work,

575
23:18.640 --> 23:21.500
they must be prepared to resolutely block the enemy

576
23:21.750 --> 23:24.210
and cover the main force crossing the river.

577
23:24.240 --> 23:24.890
Yes!

578
23:26.200 --> 23:26.880
Chairman,

579
23:27.400 --> 23:29.480
because of the heavy rain, the troops of the 5th Corps

580
23:29.480 --> 23:30.680
haven't gathered yet.

581
23:30.680 --> 23:31.920
Along the Kuchayuan line,

582
23:31.920 --> 23:34.240
there are only the corps headquarters and directly subordinate units.

583
23:34.240 --> 23:35.440
I'm afraid it will be difficult.

584
23:35.440 --> 23:38.480
Right now, it's not just the 5th Corps that's facing difficulties.

585
23:38.480 --> 23:40.340
It is our entire Central Red Army.

586
23:40.440 --> 23:42.590
Before the enemy's situation is clear,

587
23:42.590 --> 23:44.720
we all must be prepared

588
23:45.130 --> 23:47.330
to fight the enemy to the death.

589
25:05.410 --> 25:06.170
Sir,

590
25:06.800 --> 25:08.200
when are we going to camp?

591
25:08.400 --> 25:11.020
[Zhou Hunyuan, Commander of the 2nd Column, 2nd Route Army of the Kuomintang "Pursuit and Suppression" Forces]

592
25:09.670 --> 25:11.070
How far is it to Andi Town?

593
25:12.310 --> 25:13.460
Less than 15 li.

594
25:15.860 --> 25:17.890
Come on, brothers!

595
25:28.800 --> 25:37.390
[Station of the Second Bureau of the Military Commission, Shatu Town, Guizhou]

596
25:29.930 --> 25:30.900
Comrades.

597
25:31.720 --> 25:33.070
This Kangxi Dictionary

598
25:33.790 --> 25:37.000
has a total of 47,035 characters

599
25:37.720 --> 25:39.070
and 214 radicals.

600
25:39.550 --> 25:41.790
Thousands of these characters

601
25:42.160 --> 25:44.490
have been compiled into telegraph codes.

602
25:44.510 --> 25:46.640
Among these thousands of characters,

603
25:46.640 --> 25:50.070
only one character has homophones but no identical tone.

604
25:50.570 --> 25:53.130
Does anyone know which character it is?

605
26:04.230 --> 26:05.290
Ming (Life/Fate).

606
26:05.480 --> 26:06.280
That's right.

607
26:06.660 --> 26:07.500
It's Ming.

608
26:08.070 --> 26:09.480
We are all materialists

609
26:10.200 --> 26:11.660
and don't believe in fate,

610
26:11.830 --> 26:14.550
but life truly exists.

611
26:15.160 --> 26:16.200
Whenever our Red Army

612
26:16.200 --> 26:18.110
is hanging by a thread,

613
26:18.830 --> 26:19.960
this character Ming

614
26:20.160 --> 26:22.350
is in our own hands.

615
26:22.920 --> 26:24.520
This time, our Second Bureau

616
26:24.790 --> 26:27.590
must ensure nothing goes wrong.

617
26:28.100 --> 26:28.900
Comrades.

618
26:30.960 --> 26:31.620
Let's do it!

619
26:31.680 --> 26:32.480
Yes!

620
26:43.510 --> 26:44.160
Zeng.

621
26:45.710 --> 26:46.630
Zeng.

622
26:47.480 --> 26:48.610
Come and take a look.

623
26:48.920 --> 26:50.510
This is the telegram Chiang Kai-shek

624
26:50.510 --> 26:52.240
sent to Zhou and Wu a few days ago.

625
26:52.240 --> 26:54.370
Try to get a feel for the writing style.

626
26:59.740 --> 27:00.500
I got it.

627
27:00.590 --> 27:01.450
Take this down.

628
27:04.590 --> 27:06.450
Brothers Qianchu (Zhou Hunyuan)

629
27:06.720 --> 27:08.160
and Wusheng (Wu Qiwei).

630
27:10.110 --> 27:10.920
Is there a problem?

631
27:10.840 --> 27:13.790
[Cao Xiangren, Section Chief of the Second Bureau, Central Revolutionary Military Commission]

632
27:12.030 --> 27:13.270
In his previous telegrams,

633
27:13.270 --> 27:14.640
he directly addressed them as

634
27:14.640 --> 27:16.140
Commander Zhou and Commander Wu.

635
27:16.140 --> 27:17.970
I think Zeng used it well.

636
27:18.550 --> 27:19.640
Chiang Kai-shek

637
27:19.790 --> 27:20.920
is good at rhetoric.

638
27:21.640 --> 27:22.900
The more anxious he is,

639
27:22.920 --> 27:25.720
the more he likes to get close to his subordinates.

640
27:25.960 --> 27:29.290
Early this month, he urged Wan Yaohuang to go to Lubanchang.

641
27:29.750 --> 27:31.510
Wan was just a Division Commander,

642
27:31.510 --> 27:32.840
but he still called him brother,

643
27:32.840 --> 27:35.100
calling him Brother Wuqiao (Yaohuang).

644
27:35.230 --> 27:35.840
Right?

645
27:36.120 --> 27:36.990
Continue.

646
27:38.750 --> 27:39.510
Top secret.

647
27:40.510 --> 27:43.480
According to aerial reconnaissance,

648
27:43.680 --> 27:48.720
a group of bandits is feigning a move south towards the Wujiang River,

649
27:49.250 --> 27:54.450
while the main force is accelerating westward.

650
27:54.880 --> 27:55.510
Good.

651
27:56.010 --> 27:57.270
Add another sentence.

652
27:58.310 --> 27:59.030
Therefore,

653
27:59.440 --> 28:03.240
continue to advance rapidly westward along the original route.

654
28:04.130 --> 28:05.850
Do not change course or delay.

655
28:06.590 --> 28:07.790
Strengthen the tone.

656
28:07.830 --> 28:11.720
Do not change course or delay without authorization.

657
29:05.190 --> 29:06.950
Brothers Qianchu and Wusheng.

658
29:07.350 --> 29:08.070
Top secret.

659
29:08.400 --> 29:10.400
According to aerial reconnaissance,

660
29:10.400 --> 29:13.240
a group of bandits is feigning a move south towards the Wujiang River,

661
29:13.240 --> 29:15.900
while the main force is accelerating westward.

662
29:15.960 --> 29:16.620
Therefore,

663
29:16.830 --> 29:19.030
continue to advance rapidly westward along the original route.

664
29:19.030 --> 29:21.830
Do not change course or delay without authorization.

665
29:21.830 --> 29:23.510
Please travel day and night.

666
29:23.740 --> 29:26.810
You must arrive at the Panshui and Xinchang line by tomorrow.

667
29:26.810 --> 29:29.070
To annihilate these bandits in Guizhou,

668
29:29.340 --> 29:31.640
I hope you will strictly order your troops to comply.

669
29:31.640 --> 29:32.610
Personally written by Zhongzheng (Chiang Kai-shek).

670
29:32.610 --> 29:35.070
Sealed and sent between 3 and 5 a.m. on the 31st.

671
29:35.070 --> 29:35.830
Leaders.

672
29:36.440 --> 29:38.570
Are there any other changes to be made?

673
29:38.610 --> 29:39.330
No changes.

674
29:40.160 --> 29:41.070
It looks pretty real.

675
29:41.070 --> 29:43.470
When one's heart is devoted to an art, the art will surely be perfected.

676
29:43.470 --> 29:44.270
Why change it?

677
29:44.830 --> 29:46.270
Whether this telegram works or not,

678
29:46.270 --> 29:48.470
let Zhou Hunyuan and Wu Qiwei judge.

679
29:49.900 --> 29:51.700
Yes, I will send it immediately!

680
29:54.650 --> 29:55.250
Bocheng.

681
29:55.450 --> 29:55.820
Here.

682
29:56.030 --> 29:57.680
Is our advance unit for crossing the river

683
29:57.680 --> 29:58.440
ready?

684
29:58.640 --> 30:02.970
The 3rd Regiment of the 1st Red Division has reached the designated position.

685
30:06.810 --> 30:08.300
Crossing the river in this weather

686
30:08.300 --> 30:09.700
requires great courage.

687
30:09.790 --> 30:11.170
Who is in charge of ideological work?

688
30:11.170 --> 30:12.960
To ensure the advance unit

689
30:13.160 --> 30:14.310
successfully crosses the river,

690
30:14.310 --> 30:16.230
Lin and Nie specially sent the Head of the Organization Department of the Corps Political Department,

691
30:16.230 --> 30:18.830
Comrade Xiao Hua, to command at the front line.

692
30:18.880 --> 30:19.450
Good.

693
30:20.600 --> 30:22.030
Xiao Hua became the Division Political Commissar

694
30:22.030 --> 30:25.600
of the Young Communist International Division at the age of seventeen.

695
30:25.600 --> 30:27.150
His ideological work is top-notch.

696
30:27.150 --> 30:29.550
Lin and Nie made the best use of his talents.

697
30:34.550 --> 30:36.460
Later intelligence confirmed that

698
30:36.460 --> 30:38.760
this telegram, which Chiang Kai-shek never knew about until his death,

699
30:38.760 --> 30:41.040
marked "Personally written by Zhongzheng,"

700
30:41.040 --> 30:43.770
completely convinced Zhou Hunyuan and Wu Qiwei.

701
30:44.080 --> 30:45.620
They strictly followed the telegraphic order,

702
30:45.620 --> 30:46.580
made no stops,

703
30:47.260 --> 30:50.240
and rushed to the Panshui and Xinchang area overnight.

704
30:50.240 --> 30:51.460
This saved the Central Red Army

705
30:51.460 --> 30:53.740
from a devastating disaster

706
30:54.330 --> 30:56.690
and won time and space for the Red Army's next move

707
30:56.690 --> 30:58.890
to cross the Wujiang River to the south.

708
30:59.110 --> 30:59.790
Afterwards,

709
30:59.400 --> 31:03.790
[Tiziyan Ferry Crossing, Northern shore of Wujiang River, Guizhou]

710
31:00.200 --> 31:02.000
Zeng Xisheng strictly observed discipline

711
31:02.000 --> 31:03.410
and kept this secret

712
31:03.590 --> 31:06.190
until the last moment of his life.

713
31:16.430 --> 31:18.230
The Communist army is coming up!

714
31:38.590 --> 31:39.590
Comrades,

715
31:39.820 --> 31:41.170
we are the advance unit!

716
31:41.410 --> 31:43.120
We would rather die than turn back!

717
31:43.120 --> 31:45.780
Director Xiao and the comrades are watching us!

718
31:45.920 --> 31:46.830
Charge!

719
32:39.510 --> 32:40.270
Comrades,

720
32:40.600 --> 32:43.640
when charging, we must learn from the advance unit!

721
32:43.940 --> 32:45.670
Only by bravely defeating the enemy

722
32:45.670 --> 32:47.990
can we open a gap for the main force!

723
32:48.460 --> 32:50.140
Turning back or hesitating

724
32:49.370 --> 32:52.170
[Xiao Hua, Director of the Organization Department of the Political Department of the 1st Red Army Corps]

725
32:50.880 --> 32:52.330
is equal to suicide!

726
33:02.190 --> 33:04.480
Third Red Regiment, listen to my command!

727
33:04.480 --> 33:05.880
Everyone cross the river

728
33:05.960 --> 33:07.480
and seize the ferry crossing!

729
33:07.480 --> 33:08.880
Left turn!

730
33:09.880 --> 33:11.230
Double time, march!

731
33:19.030 --> 33:21.240
From March 31, 1935,

732
33:21.240 --> 33:22.400
to April 1,

733
33:22.880 --> 33:25.000
except for the 9th Red Army Corps, which had too long a journey

734
33:25.000 --> 33:27.000
and failed to cross the river on time,

735
33:27.000 --> 33:28.870
according to the instructions of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission,

736
33:28.870 --> 33:31.470
staying on the north bank to pin down the enemy,

737
33:31.830 --> 33:32.960
the Central Red Army,

738
33:32.960 --> 33:34.810
the 1st, 3rd, and 5th Corps,

739
33:34.840 --> 33:36.630
and the Military Commission Column,

740
33:36.630 --> 33:38.960
successively crossed from Datang, Jiangkou,

741
33:38.960 --> 33:41.330
and Tiziyan ferry crossings to the south of the Wujiang River,

742
33:41.330 --> 33:43.740
leaving the 400,000 Kuomintang pursuit troops

743
33:43.740 --> 33:45.870
on the north bank of the Wujiang River.

744
33:46.000 --> 33:47.030
They broke out of Chiang Kai-shek's

745
33:47.030 --> 33:48.920
carefully designed encirclement

746
33:48.920 --> 33:51.030
in northern and western Guizhou.

747
33:52.970 --> 33:55.400
During the crossing of the Wujiang River to the south,

748
33:55.400 --> 33:57.980
the legendary hero of our party's hidden front,

749
33:57.980 --> 33:59.380
Comrade Qian Zhuangfei,

750
33:59.950 --> 34:01.590
lost contact with the main force

751
34:01.590 --> 34:03.370
while dodging enemy bombing.

752
34:04.330 --> 34:07.350
The Central Committee sent people to look for him many times but failed.

753
34:07.350 --> 34:08.440
Later, after extensive research and verification

754
34:08.440 --> 34:10.840
by relevant departments and experts,

755
34:11.360 --> 34:13.190
it was determined by the Party History Research Center of the CPC Central Committee

756
34:13.190 --> 34:16.070
and the Ministry of State Security

757
34:16.230 --> 34:17.520
that Comrade Qian Zhuangfei

758
34:17.520 --> 34:20.080
sacrificed his life on April 1, 1935,

759
34:20.120 --> 34:23.250
in Houshan Township, Jinsha County, Guizhou Province.

760
34:24.710 --> 34:26.830
On April 1, 2005,

761
34:27.440 --> 34:29.030
the Qian Zhuangfei Martyrs Cemetery,

762
34:29.030 --> 34:31.670
located in Guishan Village, Houshan Township, Jinsha County,

763
34:31.670 --> 34:35.020
where the martyr sacrificed his life, was officially completed.

764
34:35.020 --> 34:36.429
It was awarded the titles of

765
34:36.429 --> 34:39.030
National Security Education Base

766
34:39.300 --> 34:42.230
and Guizhou Provincial Patriotism Education Base.

767
34:52.020 --> 34:57.290
[Mao Guangxiang Mansion, Guiyang, Guizhou]

768
34:56.889 --> 34:57.680
Boling (Xue Yue).

769
34:57.680 --> 34:58.990
He is in a fit of anger.

770
35:02.820 --> 35:03.910
Reporting to the Generalissimo!

771
35:03.910 --> 35:04.840
Boling is here.

772
35:05.610 --> 35:06.440
Come in.

773
35:06.540 --> 35:07.340
Yes!

774
35:13.650 --> 35:15.850
Tens of thousands of Communist soldiers...

775
35:15.850 --> 35:17.870
They've been crossing the river for three days.

776
35:17.870 --> 35:19.440
Where are your river defenses?

777
35:19.440 --> 35:20.370
Generalissimo.

778
35:20.450 --> 35:21.520
We encountered a heavy rainstorm.

779
35:21.520 --> 35:23.780
Didn't it rain on the Communist army too?

780
35:27.420 --> 35:28.710
You racked your brains

781
35:28.780 --> 35:30.580
setting up defenses for so long,

782
35:30.770 --> 35:32.010
only to bring the Communist army

783
35:32.010 --> 35:34.030
right under my nose!

784
35:35.430 --> 35:37.880
I am willing to accept punishment!

785
35:42.180 --> 35:43.330
Deceiving subordinates,

786
35:43.330 --> 35:44.590
deceiving superiors,

787
35:44.810 --> 35:46.360
lazy and slack,

788
35:46.980 --> 35:48.150
and perfunctory!

789
35:48.860 --> 35:50.060
With such ignorance,

790
35:50.550 --> 35:52.150
how can we have a revolution?

791
35:54.150 --> 35:54.930
Generalissimo.

792
35:54.930 --> 35:57.110
Right now, the priority is to reorganize the army

793
35:57.110 --> 35:58.220
and pursue the Communist army.

794
35:58.220 --> 35:59.380
Then tell me,

795
35:59.630 --> 36:01.670
is the Communist army fleeing west

796
36:01.670 --> 36:02.630
or east?

797
36:02.830 --> 36:04.440
Without more detailed intelligence,

798
36:04.440 --> 36:06.030
I dare not jump to conclusions.

799
36:06.030 --> 36:06.710
But I think

800
36:07.000 --> 36:08.510
the most urgent task is to quickly send

801
36:08.510 --> 36:10.190
Sun Du's column and Wu Qiwei's column

802
36:10.190 --> 36:11.190
to seize Zhenxiwei.

803
36:11.190 --> 36:11.800
Also,

804
36:11.820 --> 36:14.320
order Zhou Hunyuan's column to rush to the north bank of the Wujiang River

805
36:14.320 --> 36:15.850
to form a new encirclement.

806
36:17.840 --> 36:18.630
All right!

807
36:18.730 --> 36:20.390
Just follow your current idea

808
36:20.510 --> 36:21.350
and make the arrangements.

809
36:21.350 --> 36:21.890
Yes!

810
36:25.220 --> 36:26.140
Come back!

811
36:29.360 --> 36:29.960
Have that

812
36:29.960 --> 36:31.230
Regiment Commander of the 313th Regiment, 53rd Division,

813
36:31.230 --> 36:32.790
who is responsible for river defense,

814
36:32.790 --> 36:33.720
and his adjutant

815
36:33.920 --> 36:35.580
dismissed and investigated!

816
36:36.880 --> 36:37.400
Yes!

817
36:43.250 --> 36:44.180
Generalissimo.

818
36:44.800 --> 36:46.440
Given the current military situation,

819
36:46.440 --> 36:47.580
should the speech originally scheduled

820
36:47.580 --> 36:49.020
at the Guiyang welcome meeting

821
36:49.020 --> 36:49.990
be postponed?

822
36:50.150 --> 36:50.840
No.

823
36:51.230 --> 36:52.890
The more critical the time is,

824
36:53.310 --> 36:54.750
the more we need to encourage the people

825
36:54.750 --> 36:55.810
and reassure them.

826
36:56.090 --> 36:56.820
Understood.

827
36:56.920 --> 36:59.180
Has the topic of the speech been decided?

828
36:59.280 --> 37:00.360
According to your wishes,

829
37:00.360 --> 37:01.630
the topic of the speech is

830
37:01.630 --> 37:05.000
"How Guizhou Should Realize the Three Principles of the People."

831
37:05.000 --> 37:05.920
Good.

832
37:06.070 --> 37:07.200
This is a good topic.

833
37:08.110 --> 37:11.110
We must talk about the Three Principles of the People.

834
37:14.940 --> 37:19.100
[Qiannan Region, Guizhou]

835
37:17.920 --> 37:18.890
How rare.

836
37:19.480 --> 37:21.180
The weather has finally cleared up.

837
37:21.180 --> 37:21.820
Yes.

838
37:22.210 --> 37:24.540
They say in Guizhou there are no three consecutive sunny days,

839
37:24.540 --> 37:25.730
and no three feet of flat land.

840
37:25.730 --> 37:27.030
It seems to be true.

841
37:27.840 --> 37:30.100
We must look at problems dialectically.

842
37:30.150 --> 37:32.150
It is precisely because there are no three consecutive sunny days

843
37:32.150 --> 37:32.820
that enemy planes

844
37:32.820 --> 37:34.420
won't harass us all the time.

845
37:34.960 --> 37:37.000
It is precisely because there are no three feet of flat land

846
37:37.000 --> 37:38.150
that the Kuomintang's mechanized troops

847
37:38.150 --> 37:39.080
and their wheels

848
37:39.190 --> 37:40.770
can't race with us.

849
37:41.630 --> 37:44.160
When it comes to walking, they are far behind.

850
37:45.440 --> 37:46.320
Chairman.

851
37:46.960 --> 37:47.960
Comrade Bocheng.

852
37:51.070 --> 37:51.800
Leaders.

853
37:52.070 --> 37:53.280
The enemy situation has changed.

854
37:53.280 --> 37:55.130
The Second Bureau just received intelligence

855
37:55.130 --> 37:56.230
that Chiang Kai-shek has ordered

856
37:56.230 --> 37:58.410
Sun Du's column and Wu Qiwei's column

857
37:58.440 --> 37:59.570
to seize Zhenxiwei.

858
37:59.920 --> 38:03.920
Zhou Hunyuan is also moving towards the north bank of the Wujiang River.

859
38:06.590 --> 38:08.400
What's the situation with the Hunan Army in the east?

860
38:08.400 --> 38:09.480
No movement for now.

861
38:09.480 --> 38:10.320
But I believe

862
38:10.700 --> 38:13.890
that Chiang Kai-shek is still guarding against us going to western Hunan,

863
38:13.890 --> 38:15.820
so he dares not move the Hunan Army.

864
38:16.400 --> 38:17.150
So,

865
38:17.700 --> 38:18.780
Guiyang is empty.

866
38:19.760 --> 38:21.110
Currently, near Guiyang,

867
38:21.110 --> 38:23.840
there is only Guo Siyan's 99th Division of the Central Army.

868
38:23.840 --> 38:25.100
With a total strength of four regiments,

869
38:25.100 --> 38:26.950
it is far from enough for city defense.

870
38:26.950 --> 38:27.880
Now that we have a chance,

871
38:27.880 --> 38:30.280
it wouldn't hurt to put Chiang in check.

872
38:30.730 --> 38:31.520
Right.

873
38:31.830 --> 38:34.590
Use a portion of our forces to feign an attack on Xifeng,

874
38:34.590 --> 38:35.880
making it look like we are heading to western Hunan

875
38:35.880 --> 38:38.150
to join forces with the 2nd and 6th Corps.

876
38:38.610 --> 38:41.140
Then the main force will pass through Xifeng,

877
38:41.200 --> 38:44.320
turn towards Zhazuo and Gouchang,

878
38:44.880 --> 38:45.760
and head to Guiyang

879
38:45.760 --> 38:47.890
to knock on the Generalissimo's door.

880
38:49.020 --> 38:50.360
Sun Tzu's The Art of War says,

881
38:50.360 --> 38:51.610
"The highest form of generalship is to balk the enemy's plans;

882
38:51.610 --> 38:52.750
the next best is to prevent the junction of the enemy's forces;

883
38:52.750 --> 38:53.700
the next is to attack the enemy's army in the field;

884
38:53.700 --> 38:55.150
and the worst policy of all is to besiege walled cities."

885
38:55.150 --> 38:55.800
Chairman,

886
38:55.930 --> 38:58.430
which strategy does this knocking on the door belong to?

887
38:58.430 --> 39:00.560
I haven't read Sun Tzu's The Art of War.

888
39:00.800 --> 39:01.670
This move,

889
39:02.130 --> 39:05.590
let's just call it "harass the enemy when they are stationed."

890
39:13.710 --> 39:14.840
Besides the sudden attack on Xifeng

891
39:14.840 --> 39:16.030
by the main force of the Communist army,

892
39:16.030 --> 39:16.780
the air force also reported

893
39:16.780 --> 39:18.490
that about 80 li southeast of Guiyang,

894
39:18.490 --> 39:20.840
traces of the Communist army were also found.

895
39:20.840 --> 39:22.480
How many main forces does the Communist army have?

896
39:22.480 --> 39:24.030
The specific situation is still unclear,

897
39:24.030 --> 39:25.090
but in my analysis,

898
39:25.230 --> 39:27.000
their actions are nothing more than two possibilities.

899
39:27.000 --> 39:27.440
One.

900
39:27.750 --> 39:28.980
Feign an attack on Xifeng and launch a surprise attack on Guiyang.

901
39:28.980 --> 39:29.350
Two.

902
39:29.370 --> 39:30.960
Feign an attack on Guiyang, intending to advance east,

903
39:30.960 --> 39:31.880
exit eastern Guizhou, enter western Hunan,

904
39:31.880 --> 39:33.150
and join forces with He Long's troops.

905
39:33.150 --> 39:34.890
No matter what the true intention of the Communist army is,

906
39:34.890 --> 39:36.690
it will still endanger Guiyang.

907
39:36.890 --> 39:37.820
The top priority

908
39:38.010 --> 39:39.760
is still to ensure the safety of Guiyang.

909
39:39.760 --> 39:40.400
Of course.

910
39:40.630 --> 39:42.320
Zunyi and Guiyang are different.

911
39:42.320 --> 39:43.380
If Guiyang is lost,

912
39:43.510 --> 39:44.640
how will we deal with

913
39:44.720 --> 39:46.110
domestic public opinion?

914
39:46.110 --> 39:47.310
If it spreads abroad,

915
39:47.450 --> 39:49.380
the Party will lose all its face!

916
39:50.380 --> 39:52.520
I implore you to leave as soon as possible,

917
39:52.520 --> 39:53.290
just in case.

918
39:53.550 --> 39:55.360
I can't consider this issue right now.

919
39:55.360 --> 39:57.280
Compared to Guiyang,

920
39:57.470 --> 39:59.530
my personal safety is not important!

921
40:08.110 --> 40:09.190
Around Guiyang,

922
40:09.320 --> 40:10.580
what troops do we have?

923
40:10.710 --> 40:11.880
Currently, the only ones that can be mobilized

924
40:11.880 --> 40:13.340
are Guo Siyan's 99th Division,

925
40:13.340 --> 40:14.490
with a strength of four regiments.

926
40:14.490 --> 40:16.750
Most of them are guarding outside the city.

927
40:16.750 --> 40:18.330
The rest are inside the city,

928
40:18.330 --> 40:21.660
and only two regiments of military police can be mobilized.

929
40:22.840 --> 40:24.100
I really didn't expect

930
40:24.550 --> 40:25.920
that before this General Special-Class uniform

931
40:25.920 --> 40:27.880
even got warm on me,

932
40:28.090 --> 40:31.020
I would reach the point of having no troops to deploy!

933
40:31.380 --> 40:32.090
Also,

934
40:32.590 --> 40:33.400
Zhou and Wu's two columns

935
40:33.400 --> 40:35.280
are still a certain distance from Guiyang.

936
40:35.280 --> 40:37.760
I'm afraid it's too late.

937
40:38.000 --> 40:39.310
Who is closest to Guiyang?

938
40:39.310 --> 40:40.640
Sun Du, the Yunnan Army.

939
40:40.920 --> 40:41.590
Where is he?

940
40:41.970 --> 40:43.600
Under your repeated urging,

941
40:43.860 --> 40:46.210
the 2nd Brigade of the vanguard of Sun Du's column

942
40:46.210 --> 40:48.000
has already arrived at Zhenxiwei.

943
40:48.000 --> 40:50.490
The 7th Brigade has arrived at the Yachi River crossing.

944
40:50.490 --> 40:51.930
The remaining rearguard, the 5th Brigade,

945
40:51.930 --> 40:53.550
is expected to arrive in Qianxi today.

946
40:53.550 --> 40:54.200
Good.

947
40:54.800 --> 40:55.800
Send Sun Du a telegraphic order.

948
40:55.800 --> 40:57.280
Tell him to keep the men in gear and horses saddled,

949
40:57.280 --> 40:59.210
and march to Guiyang immediately!

950
40:59.330 --> 40:59.980
Yes!

951
41:18.940 --> 41:19.870
Generalissimo.

952
41:20.130 --> 41:20.920
Speak.

953
41:21.920 --> 41:23.320
I know a small path

954
41:23.340 --> 41:25.340
that leads directly to the airport.

955
41:27.250 --> 41:28.290
What do you mean?

956
41:30.150 --> 41:31.520
A great battle is imminent!

957
41:31.520 --> 41:33.120
Are you asking me to run away?

958
41:33.920 --> 41:35.180
What are you thinking?

959
41:35.260 --> 41:35.990
You often say

960
41:36.440 --> 41:38.400
that we must prepare for a rainy day.

961
41:38.400 --> 41:39.800
Therefore, I believe

962
41:40.630 --> 41:41.560
that as a leader,

963
41:42.180 --> 41:43.910
you cannot afford any mishaps.

964
41:44.110 --> 41:45.480
If anything happens to you,

965
41:45.480 --> 41:47.680
who will lead the National Revolution?

966
41:57.260 --> 41:59.670
It seems you've already prepared for this.

967
42:00.170 --> 42:00.890
Yes.

968
42:01.320 --> 42:03.250
I have already checked with Wang Tianxi,

969
42:03.250 --> 42:05.070
the Guiyang Garrison Commander.

970
42:05.070 --> 42:06.760
This path is absolutely secret.

971
42:06.760 --> 42:08.620
I have arranged a reliable guide,

972
42:08.800 --> 42:10.130
twelve fast horses, and two sedan chairs,

973
42:10.130 --> 42:11.460
ready at your disposal.

974
42:14.410 --> 42:17.230
Suppress the Communists, suppress the Communists.

975
42:17.230 --> 42:19.910
To think it has come to this.

976
42:21.850 --> 42:24.710
The only one who can consider things so thoroughly,

977
42:25.160 --> 42:26.290
Cixiu (Chen Cheng),

978
42:27.910 --> 42:29.000
is always you.

979
42:41.360 --> 42:42.400
Comrade Zedong!

980
42:43.400 --> 42:44.330
Comrade Zedong.

981
42:45.010 --> 42:46.340
We have the latest news.

982
42:46.800 --> 42:48.580
At dawn today, the 9th Red Army Corps,

983
42:48.580 --> 42:50.260
in the Laomukong area on the upper reaches of the Wujiang River,

984
42:50.260 --> 42:52.400
ambushed Wei Jinyong's Guizhou Army.

985
42:52.990 --> 42:54.670
They originally planned to annihilate three enemy regiments,

986
42:54.670 --> 42:55.950
but five regiments showed up.

987
42:55.950 --> 42:57.210
They took them all down

988
42:57.480 --> 42:59.300
and captured a large amount of weapons, equipment, and supplies.

989
42:59.300 --> 42:59.860
Great.

990
43:00.350 --> 43:02.070
With the Central Army busy heading south,

991
43:02.070 --> 43:03.460
the 9th Corps is much more at ease.
